  "storyId": "B-da14",
  "name": "combination-review-rule-doc",
  "title": "Document merge-time combination-review rule for parallel framework stories",
  "description": "The B-8db9 hotfix on 2026-05-15 fixed a CRITICAL bypass that B-cf60 and B-4b22 formed only after both merged to main — each passed single-story review independently. Single-story review structurally cannot see cross-story interaction defects where two locally-correct stories combine into a global hole. Capture this as a durable process rule in the truth-source docs: when multiple process-framework stories (classifier / gate policy / command entry guards / auto-commit / DONE merge semantics) merge to main in parallel, run a read-only combination review over the combined state. This is advisory process discipline scoped to process-framework stories only — not a new CLI gate, not imposed on ordinary business stories. Doc-only change to CLAUDE.md and/or docs/requirements/decisions/story-lifecycle.md.",
